// An alias that names itself, directly or through other aliases, is E0322, reported once at
// the first alias of the cycle, also when it closes more than one cycle (OPEN_QUESTIONS P5).
// An alias names a type only, so in an expression or a pattern it is E0201, also for
// `System`, which it can't build (issue #11). A `pub` alias or function may not name a
// private type in any part of its type, a function type's included (§3). An alias defined
// twice, or named like another item, is E0202, and a rejected alias isn't reported again
// where it is used (REFERENCE §15.1). Aliases take no type arguments yet.
